  "description": "The singer trainee Pyeong-Hwa who appeared in front of Woo-Joo, a boy who had lost interest in his twisted life, was more than anything a fun, exciting, and shining being. Woo-Joo, who thought it was enough to just watch Pyeong-Hwa debut from the side, soon came to have a goal of standing next to him. He began to develop precious feelings for Pyeong-Hwa who approached him without hesitation, and those feelings built up and built up, eventually becoming a greed called 'love'. \n\n *'I wish you would never know my heart. But I wish you knew.'*\n\nBut he knows. That it shouldn't be like that. He doesn't want to be a nuisance to Pyeong-Hwa who said he would not date before or after his debut. So how is Pyeong-Hwa's heart moving now? As he learns about the sweat and tears hidden behind the splendid stage, and the other side of the world he thought was only beautiful, Woo-Joo cannot leave Pyeong-Hwa's side. \n\nA love story between boys with many wounds. \n\n(Source: KakaoPage, translated)",
